# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Secrets
#
# `.env` alone was not enough: `.env.production` is the name the sample files
# actually tell you to use, and it would have been committed with your API keys
# in it. Ignore every .env variant, then add back the two that are meant to be
# shared — they contain placeholders, not values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
# (env.production.sample has no leading dot, so no pattern above touches it.)

# Data
#
# Everything the app stores lives in backend/data/: the SQLite database and its
# -wal/-shm companions, plus anything left over from the JSON era. All of it
# holds real people's names, emails, phone numbers, LinkedIn profiles, full work
# histories and the job descriptions they applied against — none of it belongs
# in a repository.
#
# Ignoring the directory rather than listing file patterns means a new kind of
# file appearing in there is private by default, which is the right way round
# for a folder that holds personal data.
backend/data/*
!backend/data/.gitkeep

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
npm-debug.log*

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
